  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">URDMC - LIVELIHOODS</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda Refugee and Disaster Management Council (URDMC) is a registered Ugandan-based non-governmental organization. The organization was founded in 2012 with the aim of protecting and promoting rights of refugees, asylum seekers and internally displaced persons. Currently, URDMC has field offices in Lamwo, Adjumani, Yumbe (Bidididi) with Head office in Arua City.
With over 10 years of experience and a mandate to implement humanitarian and development programme, URDMC had 4 project in 20221 In West Nile,funded by UNHCR, LWF, OXFAM and VIVO.  Currently, responding to the conflict induced humanitarian needs in West Nile including  Arua, Biddibidi Adjumani and Lamwo. In 2021, URDMC Implemented Youth skilling project component of entrepreneurship and financial inclusion targeting 750 youth in Imvepi settlement. URDMC has a tested and proven capacity in livelihood implementation with precise interventions and approaches to date. Additionally, in 2018-2019 implemented sustainable livelihoods in Lamwo, Adjumaniand Moyo with funding from UNHCR, 2016-2018 Livelihoods funded by Joint aids Management (JAM),  2016-2018, Emergency Food Security and Vulnerable Livelihoods for Refugees in Bidibidi (Yumbe) funded by Oxfam. URDMC have experience in inplementing and managing a  zoning project with multiple districts,different beneficiaries and the geographical context. With the fully placed Project and financial management team in place, over years URDMC have demostrated  a great improvement in the management of its business including putting in place the internal control system that guide the fund utilisation and management.
Vision: &#x201c;A nationally led organization with adequate and sustained capacity to lead in the protection of refugees&#x2019; rights and people affected byconflicts and disasters.&#x201d;
Mission: To promote and protect the rights of people who have been forced to flee their countries or their homes regardless of their race, religion, nationality or politicalaffiliations.
URDMC thematic areas includes; protection, Livelihood, Environment and energy and SGBV.
 URDMC Contribution in the project
&#x2022; Capacity building of women and youth groups on good agronomic practices, value addition, post-harvest handling, marketing, group dynamics) as community producer groups
&#x2022;  Input support (climate resilient inputs, preservation of local seeds, etc)
&#x2022;  ProvideMarket linkages (with a focus on research and dissemination of market information, training of community marketing committees as well contract brokering)
&#x2022; Technical support on production, processing and marketing, aimed a fostering local government involvement (production office, commercial office and agricultural extension officers)
&#x2022;  Mapping and needs assessment on vulnerable households in project location based on agreed vulnerability criteria</narrative>
  </description>
