   <narrative xml:lang="EN">UGANDA REFUGEE &amp;  DISASTER MGT  COU</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Uganda Refugee and Disaster Management Council (URDMC) is a registered Ugandan-based Non-Governmental Organization registration No: S.5914/9502 with its Headquarter in Gulu and Field Office located on Gulu-Adjumani Road, adjacent to Pakele Police Post, Pakele Town Board.
The organization was founded in 2012 with aims of protection of refugee#s rights through Food Distribution and Ware house management. URDMC partnered with MOBAN in collaboration with GIZ International in the implementation of Peace building project within Nakivale Refugees# Settlement-Western Uganda in 2012/2013.
URDMC in close collaboration with OPM in South Western Uganda also contributed towards the emergency response for the Congolese Refugees in Matanda Transit Centre.
In partnership with Apparel Art Uganda,URDMC is supporting child mothers in Northern Uganda with the aim of economically empowering them to exercise their rights and meettheir basic needs through creative arts and designs.

The Vision is:  To be the leading organization in the protection of refugees#right and people affected by conflict and disaster#    and the  Mission is :  #To promote and protect the rights of people who havebeen forced to flee their countries or their home regardless of their race, religion, nationality or political affiliations#.

The organisation has over three (3) years# experience in working with the people affected by disaster and conflict, especially the vulnerable children, youth and women to rebuild their lives and to promote peaceful co-existence and sustainable livelihoods in the community. URDMC believes that all people are equal and have the right to determine and direct their development, and to live in dignity regardless of background, status, and tribe, political and religious affiliation</narrative>
  </participating-org>
